# Cloudflare Pages headers config: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
#
# Without this file, Cloudflare Pages applies its own default edge cache to
# static JS/CSS (observed: `Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate`,
# ~4 hours). That cache is keyed per-hostname, so entotools.com and
# entotools.org — two separate custom domains on this same Pages deployment —
# each fill and expire their edge cache independently. Right after a deploy,
# whichever domain still has an unexpired cached copy of theme.js keeps
# serving the OLD APP_VERSION for up to 4 hours, while the other domain (cache
# already expired) picks up the new version immediately. That's the version
# drift reported in issue #33.
#
# `no-cache` (not `no-store`) still lets browsers/edge cache these files, but
# forces a revalidation (conditional If-None-Match request) on every fetch —
# an unchanged file gets a cheap 304, a changed one is served immediately, so
# a deploy is visible everywhere on the next request instead of after a
# multi-hour cache window.
/*.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/*.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
